      <version name="1.1.2" author="Quaz (EON Studios)" time="2026-09-28T17:45:39Z">
        <changelog><![CDATA[DDC: the Mix knob blends the compressed signal with a dry of the same moment. The dry used to be taken before the lookahead and the oversampler, and the wet left them a few milliseconds later, so any Mix under 100 % with lookahead on was a comb filter: measured in a sandbox, a 100 Hz tone at 50 % Mix with 5 ms lookahead came out at a two-hundredth of its level; it comes out whole now. De-Esser: the normal output is no longer clamped at 0 dBFS (an undocumented limiter in REAPER's floating-point chain: a signal peaking at 2.0 came out at 1.0, now 2.0); the sidechain-monitor output keeps its clamp.]]></changelog>
        <source file="Eon_JSFX/FX/3BandEQ_ReaKit.jsfx">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mequaz-sudo/ReaKit-FX/2220dafdb102315d72a4df0f7373055a0391b611/Eon_JSFX/FX/3BandEQ_ReaKit.jsfx</source>
