      <version name="1.1.3" author="Quaz (EON Studios)" time="2026-09-28T17:54:59Z">
        <changelog><![CDATA[Saturation: no more clicks on hot transients. The curve clamped its input and its output at 0 dBFS, so in REAPER's floating-point chain anything louder was brick-wall clipped however low the Drive -- a clipped drum hit is a loud click. The curve now saturates onto its own peak, smoothly, and the output may run past 0 dBFS the way the chain allows: at Drive 10 % a signal peaking at 2.0 used to come out at 1.0 and now comes out at 1.98; at Drive 100 % the peak is exactly 1.0, as before. Also initialises once, so a knob being dragged when playback starts keeps its drag.]]></changelog>
        <source file="Eon_JSFX/FX/3BandEQ_ReaKit.jsfx">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mequaz-sudo/ReaKit-FX/994808f58069539518d03ec5122dce0a54604476/Eon_JSFX/FX/3BandEQ_ReaKit.jsfx</source>
